  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 208 AM MDT Sat Sep 26 2026\n\nWill have dry conditions continuing today with winds weakening\nquite a bit from what they were yesterday and overnight last\nnight. Will still have gusts 20 to 30 mph in the Arco Desert\nover the INL sites but most gusts under 20 mph elsewhere. Will\nhave much cooler conditions today behind the cold frontal\npassage with highs in the 50s to lower 60s high elevations and\nmainly 60s in lower elevations. The next trof approaches from\nthe west Sunday into Monday with the chance of showers and\nthunderstorms returning Sunday evening through Monday with\nalmost all activity in the eastern mountain region. Will also\nsee some in the central mountains but not expecting much\nelsewhere in the Snake River Plain or Magic Valley. Sunday will\nbe much warmer again with high temperatures well above normal\ninto the mid to upper 70s again in low elevations with cooling\nagain Monday behind the trof with highs back into the 60s and\nlower 70s again down low. The rest of the week Tuesday into next\nSaturday looks dry with seasonable temperatures a few degrees\nbelow to above average. Winds not expected to be overly\nimpactful through the forecast period as well.",
